# Badminton court finder — data and Supabase

- **Database**: [Supabase](https://supabase.com/) (Postgres). Canonical DDL for availability storage lives in [badminton-court-finder/sql/001_court_availability_slots.sql](badminton-court-finder/sql/001_court_availability_slots.sql).
- **Manual schema**: The maintainer applies DDL in the Supabase dashboard or Supabase CLI. **Do not** assume migrations have been run from this repo unless a `supabase/migrations` (or equivalent) workflow exists and the user confirms it.
- **Canonical table**: `public.court_availability_slots` — one row per court time slot with embedded venue fields (`site_key`, `venue_name`, `venue_timezone`, `session_date`, `court_name`, `slot_start`, `slot_end`, `status`, `price`, `tags`, timestamps). Natural key for upserts: `(site_key, session_date, court_name, slot_start, slot_end)`.
- **Tags**: Column `tags` (`text[]`) holds venue semantics for mobile/UI filtering; canonical list is defined in [badminton-court-finder/app/db/venue_tags.py](badminton-court-finder/app/db/venue_tags.py) and DDL patch [badminton-court-finder/sql/003_court_availability_slots_tags.sql](badminton-court-finder/sql/003_court_availability_slots_tags.sql). Vocabulary: `sport:badminton`, `environment:indoors`, `access:private`, `place_type:court`. Keep [featured_places/featured_places/repo.py](featured_places/featured_places/repo.py) `BADMINTON_COURT_VENUE_TAGS` in sync when changing tags.
- **Env (service)**: `SUPABASE_URL` + `SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` for PostgREST; RLS policies on `court_availability_slots` must allow the service’s `SELECT` / `INSERT` / `DELETE` for role `anon` (see SQL file comments). Never commit keys; load from environment only.
- **API alignment**: JSON shapes are defined in [badminton-court-finder/app/schemas/courts.py](badminton-court-finder/app/schemas/courts.py) (`AvailabilityResponse`, `CourtAvailability`, `CourtSlot`, `SlotStatus`). Keep DB `status` values in sync with `SlotStatus` (`available`, `booked`, `past`).
- **Agent behavior**: When changing persistence or schema, provide **SQL snippets** (or updates to `badminton-court-finder/sql/*.sql`) for the user to run manually—do not execute DDL against their Supabase project from here unless explicitly asked.
